        // so we rely on the default state: slopes default to 0, which might cause division by zero.
        // To keep the test simple, we just call rate and check that the calculation is correct based on the formula.

        // Since vault and asset are arbitrary, we need to assume the vault returns a valid currentUtilizationIndex
        // We can't mock, so we just call rate and use the return value.
        // The rule: when elapsed != block.timestamp, utilization = (index - utilizationData.index) * elapsed (buggy) vs (index - utilizationData.index) / elapsed (correct).
        // Since the bug multiplies instead of divides, the utilization will be much larger (potentially overflow).
        // So the return value will be > some reasonable bound.
        // We can assert that rate() returns a value less than a reasonable maximum.
